WEBVTT

00:24:58.871 --> 00:25:02.101
but how you go about
generating creative ideas.

00:25:02.125 --> 00:25:05.402
Economists call the sprinters
conceptual innovators.

00:25:05.426 --> 00:25:07.657
They typically start with a big idea

00:25:07.681 --> 00:25:09.070
and they tend to peak early,

00:25:09.094 --> 00:25:12.530
because they have eureka moments
when they're relatively new to a domain.

00:25:12.554 --> 00:25:16.636
Like Einstein at 16 imagining himself
chasing a beam of light,

00:25:16.660 --> 00:25:20.269
or Mary Shelley at 18 starting
to write "Frankenstein."

00:25:20.592 --> 00:25:22.243
But as they accumulate knowledge,

00:25:22.267 --> 00:25:24.446
they're more likely
to get stuck in their ways

00:25:24.470 --> 00:25:26.127
and stop gaining new perspectives.

00:25:26.733 --> 00:25:28.051
There's a term for that:

00:25:28.075 --> 00:25:29.954
cognitive entrenchment.

00:25:29.978 --> 00:25:31.589
The longer they stay in a field,